WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:03.467
-Our next guest is a prolific
filmmaker and screenwriter

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:06.100
who just won the New York
Film Critics Circle Award

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.701
for Best Director for his
epic action drama film "RRR,"

00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:11.501
which is currently streaming
on Netflix.

00:00:11.501 --> 00:00:13.667
Let's take a look.

00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:15.267
-[ Screams ]

00:00:15.267 --> 00:00:24.701
♪♪

00:00:24.701 --> 00:00:34.100
♪♪

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:43.534
♪♪

00:00:43.534 --> 00:00:52.968
♪♪

00:00:52.968 --> 00:00:55.100
[ Grunts ]

00:00:55.100 --> 00:01:01.701
♪♪

00:01:01.701 --> 00:01:08.234
♪♪

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:12.501
-Please welcome to the show
S.S. Rajamouli!

00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:14.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:14.934 --> 00:01:22.934
♪♪

00:01:22.934 --> 00:01:30.901
♪♪

00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:33.801
Welcome to the show, S.S.
I'm so happy to have you here.

00:01:33.801 --> 00:01:35.267
-Thank you. My pleasure.

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:37.734
-I -- The same thing happened
to me watching that clip again

00:01:37.734 --> 00:01:39.601
that happened to me
the first time I saw this movie,

00:01:39.601 --> 00:01:42.267
which is at some point
I realized my face hurt

00:01:42.267 --> 00:01:46.167
because, without knowing it,
I was just grinning ear to ear,

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:50.567
because I had never seen
anything like this film.

00:01:50.567 --> 00:01:52.868
And my only regret
is that I watched it at home.

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:54.234
I watched it on Netflix.

00:01:54.234 --> 00:01:56.100
And you --
I heard you speak about

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:59.467
what one of your films is like
on an opening weekend in India.

00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:02.000
Can you just talk about
what the crowds are like

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.400
when they see a movie like this?

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:08.934
-What we just heard now,
in 200x.

00:02:08.934 --> 00:02:14.801
Yeah, basically, the fans
will be tearing up newspapers

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:19.434
all through the night,
making huge bags of confetti,

00:02:19.434 --> 00:02:21.200
and they come to the theater.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:24.467
And the moment
the actor's name is displayed

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:25.767
or the actor comes in

00:02:25.767 --> 00:02:28.267
or they anticipate
their favorite star

00:02:28.267 --> 00:02:30.400
is coming onto the screen,

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.300
all the confetti
will be thrown into the air.

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:35.767
You won't --
You won't see the picture,

00:02:35.767 --> 00:02:39.434
and they'll be laughing
and shouting so loudly,

00:02:39.434 --> 00:02:41.868
you can't hear the sound.

00:02:41.868 --> 00:02:43.267
The projector operator,

00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:44.934
who is not supposed to meddle
with the sound,

00:02:44.934 --> 00:02:47.801
he will be increasing
the db of the sound.

00:02:47.801 --> 00:02:50.300
But still
you can't hear anything.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:53.234
-It is a -- It must be amazing,

00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:55.701
and I assume that
that is your goal, right?

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:58.467
Like, it is so -- Again,
the audacity in this film,

00:02:58.467 --> 00:03:00.467
the things I saw in this movie
that I --

00:03:00.467 --> 00:03:01.968
Again, I've seen
so many action films.

00:03:01.968 --> 00:03:04.133
There were five, six
different set pieces

00:03:04.133 --> 00:03:06.701
that went beyond
my wildest imagination

00:03:06.701 --> 00:03:08.501
of what you could accomplish.

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:11.167
That must be the goal
you set out to achieve,

00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:13.667
which is just to shock
and delight people.

00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:15.934
-Absolutely.

00:03:15.934 --> 00:03:19.601
But the initial thing
which I talked about --

00:03:19.601 --> 00:03:21.234
the confetti
and all that stuff happens

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:24.400
for almost all the star films
in the beginning.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:27.033
What I want to achieve
is that happening

00:03:27.033 --> 00:03:29.801
even after the 10th day
or the 11th day

00:03:29.801 --> 00:03:34.968
or happening outside
my country in the U.S.

00:03:34.968 --> 00:03:39.234
Not the confetti part,
but the enjoying part.

00:03:39.234 --> 00:03:45.133
And like you said, I want
my audience to be astonished

00:03:45.133 --> 00:03:48.601
and really thrilled
about the astonishment.

00:03:48.601 --> 00:03:51.067
-This is sort of
a historical epic.

00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:52.734
It takes place in 1920.

00:03:52.734 --> 00:03:54.834
We saw a couple of
freedom fighters there.

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:57.167
It's a wonderful
friendship story,

00:03:57.167 --> 00:04:00.601
and, you know, it's about them
revolting against British rule.

00:04:00.601 --> 00:04:02.367
Was this an idea you always
had in your head

00:04:02.367 --> 00:04:04.100
to do something like this?

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:07.667
-Not always,
but I had an idea of --

00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:10.734
always had an idea
of doing a multi-star.

00:04:10.734 --> 00:04:12.267
Not just bringing
the stars together

00:04:12.267 --> 00:04:14.767
but bringing
two heroes together.

00:04:14.767 --> 00:04:17.467
Right from my childhood,
I had these ideas of --

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:19.701
Whenever I read stories,
different stories,

00:04:19.701 --> 00:04:22.834
I like bringing those
heroes together and --

00:04:22.834 --> 00:04:25.234
and making up some scenes
with them.

00:04:25.234 --> 00:04:28.801
Sometimes I'd also be
in that scene in my head.

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.701
I always liked to do that.

00:04:30.701 --> 00:04:32.133
And when I saw

00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:36.234
"Inglorious Basterds"
in the theaters

00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:39.701
and when Hitler was suddenly
shot with a machine gun,

00:04:39.701 --> 00:04:43.367
I thought,
"Wow. This is really -- Wow."

00:04:43.367 --> 00:04:45.968
I mean, we know he clearly
didn't die that way,

00:04:45.968 --> 00:04:48.667
but it's fiction, you know?

00:04:48.667 --> 00:04:52.534
It's a fictional movie, and you
can take liberties with that.

00:04:52.534 --> 00:04:57.400
And, yeah, putting those
two things together is the --

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:01.033
-I will admit I had never seen
either of your stars before,

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:04.234
and yet the first time either
of them came on screen,

00:05:04.234 --> 00:05:06.767
I knew that is
a gigantic movie star.

00:05:06.767 --> 00:05:08.634
And I have to assume
I'm right about that.

00:05:08.634 --> 00:05:10.767
-Yes, they are.
They're big stars.

00:05:10.767 --> 00:05:13.334
-Were they -- I mean,
they're the most charismatic,

00:05:13.334 --> 00:05:16.167
fun-to-watch pair I've seen
in a movie in so long.

00:05:16.167 --> 00:05:18.400
Were they both on board
with this idea of,

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:22.067
"Oh, we can do this film
with S.S. where we team up

00:05:22.067 --> 00:05:26.200
and it's sort of a two-hander
as opposed to just one star"?

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.634
-I worked with them before,
and I had --

00:05:28.634 --> 00:05:30.968
We had successes,
big successes.

00:05:30.968 --> 00:05:33.968
And apart from the
professional relationship,

00:05:33.968 --> 00:05:36.400
we have a personal friendship.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:41.501
And they, too, are friends
outside their professional area.

00:05:41.501 --> 00:05:44.300
So when I wanted to do
this multi-star,

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:47.767
what I did was -- I knew
if I called one of those,

00:05:47.767 --> 00:05:51.033
he will call the other person
before I can call him.

00:05:51.033 --> 00:05:53.667
So what I did was
I just called each of them

00:05:53.667 --> 00:05:55.901
and I said, "Why don't you
come out to my place?"

00:05:55.901 --> 00:05:58.234
They didn't have an idea
of why I was --

00:05:58.234 --> 00:05:59.534
why I was calling them.

00:05:59.534 --> 00:06:01.000
So they just came over,

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:05.033
and they were surprised
to see the other in my place.

00:06:05.033 --> 00:06:06.601
And I said, "Okay, guys."

00:06:06.601 --> 00:06:08.667
I took them to my balcony
and said,

00:06:08.667 --> 00:06:10.267
"Okay, guys, I have this idea,

00:06:10.267 --> 00:06:13.234
and I'm putting this to you
both at the same time.

00:06:13.234 --> 00:06:16.067
I want you to do a multi-star
with you. Are you up for it?"

00:06:16.067 --> 00:06:17.400
I didn't tell them the story.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:19.534
I didn't tell them
what I'm going to make

00:06:19.534 --> 00:06:21.701
because I also didn't have
a clear-cut idea

00:06:21.701 --> 00:06:24.934
of what I was doing
at that point.

00:06:24.934 --> 00:06:29.234
Yeah, it was a nice coup,
and it worked.

00:06:29.234 --> 00:06:30.968
-Yeah. Well, well done.

00:06:30.968 --> 00:06:32.901
Can you tell us
about the title, "RRR"?

00:06:32.901 --> 00:06:35.033
Is that something you had
from the beginning

00:06:35.033 --> 00:06:37.367
and what those R's stand for?

00:06:37.367 --> 00:06:40.200
-[ Laughs ] That's funny.

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:43.234
That's not the title
we had in mind,

00:06:43.234 --> 00:06:45.968
and when we announced
that all three of us

00:06:45.968 --> 00:06:50.234
are going to work together,
we had to put --

00:06:50.234 --> 00:06:53.767
give out some name
to refer to the picture.

00:06:53.767 --> 00:06:57.534
So we took the first letters
of our names,

00:06:57.534 --> 00:06:59.667
Rajamouli, Rama Rao,
Ram Charan --

00:06:59.667 --> 00:07:02.767
and we just put #RRR.

00:07:02.767 --> 00:07:07.501
It was just a name
to refer to the picture,

00:07:07.501 --> 00:07:10.067
not actual the title.

00:07:10.067 --> 00:07:11.601
But the fans started
with the title.

00:07:11.601 --> 00:07:12.934
They loved the title.

00:07:12.934 --> 00:07:15.901
The distributors of our films
loved the title.

00:07:15.901 --> 00:07:18.801
They said, "This is the title."

00:07:18.801 --> 00:07:21.400
So we didn't know what to do
and said,

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:24.167
"Okay, guys.
'RRR' can't be the title."

00:07:24.167 --> 00:07:27.000
So, we have many languages
in India.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:30.033
The film is dubbed into
five languages in India itself.

00:07:30.033 --> 00:07:33.801
So we put a competition
for the audiences, for the fans,

00:07:33.801 --> 00:07:36.100
saying that you expand
the title.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:42.000
So we have that title for each
region, for each language.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:44.367
But the common title
will stay as "RRR."

00:07:44.367 --> 00:07:46.100
-You obviously are
a really established director.

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:47.701
You've had nothing but success.

00:07:47.701 --> 00:07:49.667
I would assume you've never had

00:07:49.667 --> 00:07:52.133
quite this response
from the West.

00:07:52.133 --> 00:07:53.901
What has it been like?

00:07:53.901 --> 00:07:57.200
You know, I saw you win
this award for Best Director

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:59.234
here in New York,
and, obviously,

00:07:59.234 --> 00:08:03.100
I saw footage from people
responding with great fanfare

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:05.000
as they saw it in theaters
in the States.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.300
Has this been exciting

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:08.567
as this has become sort of
a worldwide phenomenon?

00:08:08.567 --> 00:08:11.501
-"Exciting"
is an understatement.

00:08:11.501 --> 00:08:15.801
It is -- I'm in --
We are on the top of the world.

00:08:15.801 --> 00:08:18.834
I essentially make films
for Indians in India

00:08:18.834 --> 00:08:21.200
and across the globe.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:25.834
But when we started getting
appreciation from the West,

00:08:25.834 --> 00:08:27.467
our initial thought was,

00:08:27.467 --> 00:08:29.834
"These guys must be
the friends of our Indians

00:08:29.834 --> 00:08:31.267
who went to watch the film."

00:08:31.267 --> 00:08:32.601
[ Laughter ]

00:08:32.601 --> 00:08:37.100
Then as it started increasing
when the celebrities,

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:39.667
story writers, film directors,

00:08:39.667 --> 00:08:41.501
so many people
started tweeting about it,

00:08:41.501 --> 00:08:44.567
talking about it --
the film on the social media,

00:08:44.567 --> 00:08:51.100
they started championing
for the film by word of mouth,

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:54.701
we thought, "Okay,
this is growing much more."

00:08:54.701 --> 00:08:56.133
Then it released on Netflix,

00:08:56.133 --> 00:09:01.400
and it was on the top ten
for 15 consecutive weeks.

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:03.334
It released in Japan.
It's still running in Japan.

00:09:03.334 --> 00:09:07.534
This is the highest-grossing
Indian film ever in Japan.

00:09:07.534 --> 00:09:09.267
Oh, my God.

00:09:09.267 --> 00:09:10.501
-I should note a couple

00:09:10.501 --> 00:09:12.434
of Golden Globe nominations,
as well.

00:09:12.434 --> 00:09:14.868
You got that.
-Yes.

00:09:14.868 --> 00:09:17.534
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-And, you know, it is --

00:09:17.534 --> 00:09:20.234
I feel it gets so hard
to see something

00:09:20.234 --> 00:09:21.801
that you've never seen before,

00:09:21.801 --> 00:09:24.267
and that is how I felt through
the entirety of your film.

00:09:24.267 --> 00:09:26.133
It is just such a joy
to have you here.

00:09:26.133 --> 00:09:27.934
Congratulations to everything.
It's so well-deserved.

00:09:27.934 --> 00:09:29.767
I really, really appreciate it.
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:09:29.767 --> 00:09:32.434
-Thank you so much.
S.S. Rajamouli, everybody.

00:09:32.434 --> 00:09:34.934
"RRR" is currently streaming
on Netflix.

00:09:34.934 --> 00:09:36.968
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

